Bug (pre-existing since at least 0.2.0, made loud by k62): every sync – CLI `skilletor sync`, or the SessionStart hook whenever the user scope has a change – also runs the project scope in whatever directory it starts in. With no project `skilletor.json`/`skilletor.local.json` and no project lock, the project scope still writes `<dir>/.claude/.gitignore` with the fixed entries. Since k62 the report and the hook also say `.claude/.gitignore updated — commit it`, in repos that never used skilletor.

Repro (orchestrator, 2026-09-26, HOME/CODEX_HOME in temp dirs, `~/.claude/settings.json` = `{}`, user config installing one skill from a local source): `cd <git repo without .claude/>; bin/skilletor sync` → `skilletor: project scope / .claude/.gitignore updated — commit it`, `git status` shows `?? .claude/.gitignore`. Same in a plain non-git dir. The committed pre-k62 dist (c3a4191) writes the same file (entries `skilletor.local.json`, `skilletor.lock.json`), without the hint.

Fix (spec §6.4, orchestrator adds the sentence): project blocks are written only while the project scope is in use – a project `skilletor.json` or `skilletor.local.json` exists, or the project lock does (items to clean up). Otherwise nothing is written, and a skilletor block found there (litter from earlier versions) is removed – the file deleted if only the block remained. No commit hint for that cleanup. The `.agents`/`.codex` project roots follow the same rule.

Done when: tests cover no config + no lock → no file created, no hint; litter block removed (file deleted when only the block, kept otherwise); config present → block as today; lock present but config gone → block kept until the lock is empty; hook path included; full check chain green.

